CDATA[West Africa]]></category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://allafrica.com/stories/202611040426.html</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 12:56:15 GMT</pubDate><description><![CDATA[[allAfrica] Dakar -- African women's rugby made its mark at the Dakar 2026 Youth Olympic Games. At the Iba Mar Diop complex, Kenya secured gold after a spectacular final against Australia, while Madagascar took bronze. For Senegal, the host country, this first international experience opens new avenues for the development of the sport among young girls.]]></description></item><item><title><![CDATA[Africa: How Many More COPs Before Climate Promises Become Action?]]></title><link>https://allafrica.com/stories/202611040346.html</link><author>info@allafrica.com (allAfrica)</author><category><![CDATA[Africa]]></category><category><![CDATA[Food and Agriculture]]></category><category><![CDATA[Economy, Business and Finance]]></category><category><![CDATA[Climate]]></category><category><![CDATA[Environment]]></category><category><![CDATA[External Relations]]></category><category><![CDATA[International Organizations and Africa]]></category><guid isPermaLink="true">https://allafrica.com/stories/202611040346.html</guid><pubDate>Wed, 04 Nov 2026 11:27:53 GMT</pubDate><description><![CDATA[[allAfrica] Every year before COP, the same question surfaces: what is the one thing Africa needs from this summit?]]></description></item></channel></rss>